{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562879-four-fledgelings-walk-into-a-bar\u2026","id":1562879,"title":"Four Fledgelings Walk Into A Bar\u2026","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-08-08T16:43:59-07:00","id":1562879,"title":"Four Fledgelings Walk Into A Bar\u2026","content":"So this is a meta question I have and I\u2019m curious if others have thought about before. <br /> <br /> A common start for vampire games, in my experience as a player and ST at least, is that a handful of young neonates or fledglings are brought together to solve some mystery or accomplish some task that serves as an inciting incident and then the game plays out in sandbox-ish fashion as they pursue their own goals, respond to plot hooks, and deal with the consequences of their actions.<br /> <br /> My question is, would three to five (the average size of a player coterie in my experience) Fledgelings being created within a couple years of one another be an unusual event for your play cities and if so, how do you rationalize it? <br /> <br /> Some ways to justify it that occur to me:<br /> <br /> -there\u2019s actually a fairly decent amount of vampiric creation going on at all times, but most young vampires still end up biting the dust within a couple of years, so there\u2019s not much turn-over at the top<br /> <br /> -the young neonates are actually being drawn from surrounding \u2018feeder\u2019 communities, with regional vampires going to central cities to have their progeny recognized and allowed into vampiric society<br /> <br /> -it is actually unusual and there\u2019s a particular reason for why several vampires were given permission to sire within such close proximity to one another <br /> <br /> -older/traditional vampires would grumble that too many childer are being created and illegal embraces being retroactively sanctioned but this is an increasingly common fact of life in the final nights (whether because of the pressures of sect warfare, princely unwillingness to incite possible anarch/clanless retribution, general corruption/malaise, or what have you)<br /> <br /> Any other ideas that occur to you all, I\u2019d be glad to hear them, or if you think that the premise of the question is misguided","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-08T22:23:55-07:00","id":1562891,"title":"","content":"Unless the Camarilla had only recently established themselves and were looking to bring in some new blood to help kick things off, then yeah, I'd say that creating 5 new vampires at around the same time might be considered unusual.<br /> <br /> That skirts the line of a 'mass embrace' and could draw unwanted attention if several people all collectively go missing.<br /> <br /> Anarch and Sabbat games wouldn't really care about that kind of stuff though, so it's less of an issue for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-09T18:48:36-07:00","id":1562912,"title":"","content":"I think about that regularly, but usually my go to is a mix of the following, proportions varying by Chronicle:<br /> <br /> 1. Several Embraces around the same time are not actually that rare. Most Princes give most permissions like that, actually, then close the path forward years. &quot;Out of season&quot; permission is the actual outlier.<br /> <br /> 2. Friction is, indeed, a factor. Vampires die and vampires move. So while I wouldn't say many Neonates die yearly, enough do so or just go away that &quot;free spots&quot; aren't really as rare as one may think.<br /> <br /> 3. Chronicles are exceptional moments. It's not much intuitive since we trade stories and play many games, but the actual assumption isn't that our games represent typical nights or our PCs are regular vampires. You can run a game in Chicago today and still have for your game that this is the first time such a Coterie formed.<br /> <br /> 4. Destiny and fate at work, building upon the above. Any number of things may have caused this group to form. If I have an interesting idea I just play with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-09T23:43:36-07:00","id":1562926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562879-four-fledgelings-walk-into-a-bar\u2026?p=1562912#post1562912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Chronicles are exceptional moments. It's not much intuitive since we trade stories and play many games, but the actual assumption isn't that our games represent typical nights or our PCs are regular vampires. You can run a game in Chicago today and still have for your game that this is the first time such a Coterie formed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering vampires concoct plans that take decades, or even centuries to come to fruition, it does sound reasonable that there would be a considerable period in which nothing eventful happens in the city. It's not that the vampires aren't active, but rather they're in the process of getting things ready before they make their move.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}